WEBVTT

00:00:19.525 --> 00:00:21.065
(Lee Je Hoon)

00:00:21.135 --> 00:00:23.165
(Jang Hyuk Jin, Bae Yoo Ram, Kim Eui Sung, Pyo Ye Jin)

00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:37.245
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:00:37.315 --> 00:00:38.344
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:00:38.345 --> 00:00:39.345
(All people, incidents, and backgrounds...)

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:41.055
(in this drama are fictitious.)

00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:42.115
(Children and animals were filmed under guidelines.)

00:02:06.835 --> 00:02:07.975
How long have you been with the unit?

00:02:10.545 --> 00:02:11.745
Eight months, sir.

00:02:19.185 --> 00:02:20.415
The mission was a failure,

00:02:21.085 --> 00:02:22.815
and you died in action just eight months in?

00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:26.625
And you, instructor? How long have you served?

00:02:27.695 --> 00:02:30.825
- Six years. - And you died after six years too.

00:02:36.335 --> 00:02:38.005
Attacking me after you're dead doesn't count.

00:02:38.135 --> 00:02:39.205
I wasn't dead yet.

00:02:39.865 --> 00:02:41.405
I stabbed you as I was dying.

00:02:42.235 --> 00:02:43.745
Consider it my dying message.

00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:46.375
But, sir... (Support Admin Watch on
kissasia.cam or kisskh.org)

00:02:46.675 --> 00:02:49.545
What if I were to say I saw her stab you before she died?

00:02:50.145 --> 00:02:51.145
Am I going to get in trouble?

00:02:58.955 --> 00:02:59.955
What's your name?

00:03:01.155 --> 00:03:03.595
Sergeant Yoo Sun A, Counter-Terrorism Team one, sir.

00:03:05.895 --> 00:03:09.265
- Everyone, fall in! - Yes, sir! All right, fall in!

00:03:11.405 --> 00:03:13.205
Hey, on your feet.

00:03:15.635 --> 00:03:18.375
Did anything about this operation strike you as odd?

00:03:19.175 --> 00:03:20.545
Sergeant Park Jae Won, sir.

00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:25.945
Sir, I believe the hostage's safety wasn't the priority in the plan.

00:03:26.585 --> 00:03:28.485
We could've been the ones who killed the hostage.

00:03:28.785 --> 00:03:30.725
That's precisely what blinded you.

00:03:32.085 --> 00:03:35.195
One simple feint, and half of your unit was wiped out.

00:03:35.595 --> 00:03:36.595
Any idea why?

00:03:38.965 --> 00:03:40.495
Because you all assumed the hostage you took...

00:03:40.935 --> 00:03:43.295
was your get-out-of-jail-free card.

00:03:43.935 --> 00:03:47.205
You figured if things went south, you'd use them as a human shield.

00:03:47.805 --> 00:03:49.835
But if the hostage dies, the mission's a failure, right, sir?

00:03:52.345 --> 00:03:53.875
If I really intended to rescue them,

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:57.945
I'd have secured them first, not entered from the opposite side.

00:03:59.245 --> 00:04:03.415
I came through the main gate, blocked your escape and engaged.

00:04:03.985 --> 00:04:06.085
My objective for this operation...

00:04:06.755 --> 00:04:08.125
wasn't to rescue the hostage.

00:04:09.295 --> 00:04:11.225
It was to annihilate all of you,

00:04:12.465 --> 00:04:13.565
the hostage included.

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:18.505
So, if this were a real combat situation

00:04:18.865 --> 00:04:21.105
and you realised the enemy wasn't protecting the hostage,

00:04:21.835 --> 00:04:24.075
but was instead cutting off your escape routes,

00:04:25.175 --> 00:04:27.075
the very first thing you should do...

00:04:28.545 --> 00:04:29.915
was quickly get out of there.

00:04:31.945 --> 00:04:36.655
If you can't run, then with your last dying breath,

00:04:37.185 --> 00:04:39.655
take down at least one more of them...

00:04:40.055 --> 00:04:41.055
with everything you've got.

00:04:43.025 --> 00:04:46.225
Your final stand will instil fear in the enemy.

00:04:46.925 --> 00:04:48.595
And that fear will spread like wildfire,

00:04:49.435 --> 00:04:52.405
becoming a coat of armour for the rest of your team.

00:04:53.435 --> 00:04:55.475
- Understood? - Yes, sir!

00:04:55.735 --> 00:04:56.775
On that note,

00:04:57.275 --> 00:04:59.275
I want you all to learn from Sergeant Yoo's final action.

00:05:03.575 --> 00:05:06.345
Check your personnel and gear, then return to base.

00:05:07.085 --> 00:05:09.355
We'll cover the rest in the AAR.

00:05:10.185 --> 00:05:12.455
- Salute! - Unity!

00:05:14.555 --> 00:05:15.555
Unity.

00:05:16.925 --> 00:05:17.925
At ease.

00:06:49.015 --> 00:06:52.655
(Seoul 24M 5283)

00:07:07.305 --> 00:07:11.644
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:07:11.645 --> 00:07:15.975
(Taxi Driver 3)

00:07:16.275 --> 00:07:18.545
- How can I help you? - Hi.

00:07:18.945 --> 00:07:21.485
This monstrosity was delivered to my house.

00:07:24.385 --> 00:07:26.425
(Military Manpower Administration Notice of Active Duty Enlistment)

00:07:26.785 --> 00:07:27.825
Yes? So?

00:07:28.155 --> 00:07:32.365
I was honourably discharged from the military over a decade ago.

00:07:32.595 --> 00:07:34.495
All right, let me just check that for you.

00:07:34.835 --> 00:07:36.265
I'm telling you, when I saw this,

00:07:36.995 --> 00:07:38.005
I was so shocked, my heart jumped.

00:07:38.065 --> 00:07:41.835
- I'm checking. Please have a seat. - Right, sure.

00:07:45.075 --> 00:07:46.075
Mr. Park Jin Eon?

00:07:46.475 --> 00:07:47.475
Yes.

00:07:47.575 --> 00:07:48.675
(Subject eligible for active duty)

00:07:48.775 --> 00:07:49.815
But I see no record of prior service.

00:07:49.875 --> 00:07:51.185
(Building a Korea proud of its military service)

00:07:51.245 --> 00:07:52.245
What record?

00:07:52.385 --> 00:07:55.015
Your completed service record. It's not here.

00:07:58.025 --> 00:08:00.125
And what happens if there's no record?

00:08:00.185 --> 00:08:01.525
You'll have to enlist again.

00:08:01.995 --> 00:08:03.855
- Go where? - The military.

00:08:03.925 --> 00:08:04.925
No way!

00:08:06.395 --> 00:08:08.565
I'm sorry. Sorry about that.

00:08:09.335 --> 00:08:12.205
- I'm telling you, I already served! - Sir, please calm down.

00:08:12.305 --> 00:08:14.075
How am I supposed to stay calm? How?

00:08:15.675 --> 00:08:17.575
You're saying I have to enlist again just because there's no record?

00:08:18.475 --> 00:08:20.815
To someone who's already served ages ago?

00:08:21.015 --> 00:08:22.875
Wait, your enlistment date was yesterday?

00:08:23.545 --> 00:08:27.215
That makes you AWOL. We'll help you enlist immediately.

00:08:27.715 --> 00:08:30.615
What kind of twisted thing is that to say?

00:08:32.925 --> 00:08:33.925
What's going on?

00:08:34.895 --> 00:08:36.025
You're reporting for duty. Now.

00:08:36.395 --> 00:08:38.025
Reporting for duty? No, wait. Hold on!

00:08:38.095 --> 00:08:40.465
Hey, wait! I think there's been a mistake.

00:08:40.525 --> 00:08:42.335
No personal excuses.

00:08:42.395 --> 00:08:44.405
I'm telling you, I already did my time!

00:08:45.305 --> 00:08:46.305
(Active-duty enlistment)

00:08:47.005 --> 00:08:48.275
Have a good tour of duty.

00:08:49.275 --> 00:08:50.805
No! I can't go!

00:08:51.305 --> 00:08:53.045
No!

00:09:01.815 --> 00:09:03.815
- What do you mean, "no"? - I'm sorry.

00:09:03.885 --> 00:09:06.625
- Why are you screaming? - I'm sorry. I just...

00:09:07.355 --> 00:09:08.355
Go Eun.

00:09:09.025 --> 00:09:10.025
Gyeong Gu.

00:09:10.095 --> 00:09:12.195
What kind of dream makes you scream like that?

00:09:12.325 --> 00:09:14.535
Hey, look. You're breaking out in a cold sweat.

00:09:18.235 --> 00:09:20.305
It was a dream! It was all just a dream!

00:09:20.465 --> 00:09:21.605
Gosh, that was intense.

00:09:22.475 --> 00:09:24.405
Goodness. Such a drama queen.

00:09:24.905 --> 00:09:27.305
- Did you dream you got drafted? - Yes.

00:09:27.775 --> 00:09:28.775
For real?

00:09:28.845 --> 00:09:30.815
I kept saying it was a mistake, but they dragged me off to the army.

00:09:31.015 --> 00:09:33.185
- That must've been terrifying. - Totally.

00:09:35.015 --> 00:09:38.985
- Want to hear an even scarier one? - Scarier than a draft notice?

00:09:39.185 --> 00:09:40.485
Way scarier.

00:09:41.025 --> 00:09:43.725
Because this one actually happened to me.

00:09:43.825 --> 00:09:46.495
I love scary stories.

00:09:49.635 --> 00:09:52.505
Hey, where are you going? Come on.

00:10:03.175 --> 00:10:05.415
Do you really have to set the mood like this?

00:10:06.085 --> 00:10:07.145
Spooky.

00:10:08.385 --> 00:10:10.685
My senior and I...

00:10:12.085 --> 00:10:14.125
were on guard duty at the gatehouse...

00:10:15.625 --> 00:10:18.625
when over in the washroom at the HQ barracks,

00:10:19.095 --> 00:10:21.935
- a soldier was dancing like crazy. - Dancing?

00:10:21.995 --> 00:10:22.995
So my senior...

00:10:23.735 --> 00:10:24.905
asked me what I was looking at.

00:10:25.565 --> 00:10:26.565
What?

00:10:26.635 --> 00:10:29.175
I said, "See that guy over there, dancing his heart out?"

00:10:29.505 --> 00:10:32.545
He said he couldn't see anyone. But I could see him clear as day.

00:10:33.075 --> 00:10:36.375
We went back and forth all shift, and when we were relieved,

00:10:36.615 --> 00:10:38.885
we went to the command post to report in.

00:10:39.245 --> 00:10:41.855
Right after we reported in, I told them what happened.

00:10:42.485 --> 00:10:43.485
And that's when...

00:10:44.885 --> 00:10:46.025
the sergeant major...

00:10:47.325 --> 00:10:50.695
told me that ten years ago, in that exact spot,

00:10:51.825 --> 00:10:54.735
a new recruit had hanged himself.

00:10:54.995 --> 00:10:55.995
- What? - What?

00:10:56.535 --> 00:11:00.465
The way the body was swaying, it must have looked like dancing.

00:11:01.575 --> 00:11:02.575
Ever since then,

00:11:02.935 --> 00:11:07.475
they say anyone who saw the soldier has either died or gone insane.

00:11:09.175 --> 00:11:10.415
But you saw him.

00:11:11.115 --> 00:11:12.984
I guess it doesn't count if you can't see him clearly.

00:11:12.985 --> 00:11:14.855
Actually, it was quite far, so I couldn't see clearly.

00:11:15.415 --> 00:11:17.415
- I don't think so. - What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:17.485 --> 00:11:20.525
- That explains it. - Explains what?

00:11:21.325 --> 00:11:22.425
It probably followed you here.

00:11:25.025 --> 00:11:27.395
Driver Kim Do Gi! How long have you been here?

00:11:27.635 --> 00:11:30.765
I've been here the whole time. I had no chance to slip away.

00:11:31.765 --> 00:11:32.835
- Gosh. - You scared the life out of me.

00:11:32.905 --> 00:11:33.905
You were?

00:11:34.335 --> 00:11:37.975
Why lie about being followed? That's creepy.

00:11:38.075 --> 00:11:40.474
But it is true.

00:11:40.475 --> 00:11:43.045
It's probably following us now.

00:11:43.375 --> 00:11:47.415
- Are you serious? - Okay, never mind. It isn't scary.

00:11:47.485 --> 00:11:51.325
Gosh, that's not funny. It's not funny at all.

00:11:51.385 --> 00:11:52.385
Gosh.

00:11:55.055 --> 00:11:56.325
- What? - What's this?

00:11:58.825 --> 00:11:59.895
Do ghosts really exist?

00:12:07.705 --> 00:12:08.735
Captain Kim Do Gi.

00:12:15.845 --> 00:12:17.115
It's been a while. Have you been well, sir?

00:12:18.685 --> 00:12:19.685
Park Jae Won.

00:12:28.855 --> 00:12:30.555
- Have you been well? - Yes, sir.

00:12:30.855 --> 00:12:32.465
- Have you been well, sir? - Yes.

00:12:37.195 --> 00:12:39.935
I've never seen you take the afternoon off, Driver Kim.

00:12:40.635 --> 00:12:43.105
Mr. Jang is out, so I couldn't tell him.

00:12:43.275 --> 00:12:45.075
I'll let him know for you.

00:12:45.775 --> 00:12:47.545
All right, enjoy your time off. See you tomorrow.

00:12:47.875 --> 00:12:48.875
See you tomorrow.

00:12:51.915 --> 00:12:52.915
Jae Won.

00:12:53.745 --> 00:12:55.615
I told you to wait in the car. Why did you get out?

00:12:55.685 --> 00:12:57.015
I'm perfectly fine, sir.

00:12:57.685 --> 00:12:59.354
- You haven't eaten yet, have you? - No, sir.

00:12:59.355 --> 00:13:02.355
I know a few great restaurants, so let's pick one on the way.

00:13:02.425 --> 00:13:03.525
I'm good with anything, sir.

00:13:05.225 --> 00:13:07.635
Has Driver Kim Do Gi ever had a visitor here before?

00:13:08.095 --> 00:13:09.295
No, never.

00:13:09.965 --> 00:13:12.865
His rank is Master Sergeant. Gosh, that's so cool.

00:13:13.435 --> 00:13:16.135
- Driver Kim Do Gi looks so happy. - Yes.

00:13:22.675 --> 00:13:24.815
He must've been really happy to see him.

00:13:27.815 --> 00:13:29.185
Master Sergeant Park, what are you in the mood for?

00:13:29.715 --> 00:13:30.855
You still like ginseng chicken soup?

00:13:32.185 --> 00:13:35.155
- You even remember that, sir? - Of course.

00:13:35.655 --> 00:13:38.565
You and Master Sergeant Yoo insisted we go for ginseng chicken soup.

00:13:42.095 --> 00:13:43.095
What about Master Sergeant Yoo?

00:13:43.695 --> 00:13:44.735
How's she doing?

00:13:45.405 --> 00:13:48.475
You should've brought her with you. I haven't seen her in ages.

00:13:50.805 --> 00:13:53.275
I assumed you hadn't heard the news, sir.

00:13:55.815 --> 00:13:56.815
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A...

00:14:01.385 --> 00:14:02.415
is dead, sir.

00:14:15.535 --> 00:14:16.535
The thing is...

00:14:18.365 --> 00:14:21.575
That's why I came to see you. I need your signature on a petition.

00:14:25.645 --> 00:14:28.315
(Petition)

00:14:30.175 --> 00:14:31.315
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A...

00:14:32.985 --> 00:14:34.115
Where is she now?

00:14:34.815 --> 00:14:38.025
(The Late Yoo Sun A)

00:15:02.915 --> 00:15:04.945
(The Late Yoo Sun A)

00:15:13.025 --> 00:15:16.455
Mom!

00:15:23.765 --> 00:15:25.265
Will you be returning, sir?

00:15:29.605 --> 00:15:30.605
No.

00:15:31.875 --> 00:15:33.445
Please come back when this is over, sir.

00:15:36.915 --> 00:15:37.985
Even if I did come back,

00:15:38.785 --> 00:15:40.185
there's nothing left for me to teach you.

00:15:40.485 --> 00:15:41.755
Even if you have no more to teach,

00:15:42.855 --> 00:15:44.485
I still have much to learn from you, sir.

00:16:02.675 --> 00:16:04.405
I'll be waiting for your return, sir.

00:16:13.585 --> 00:16:14.585
I will...

00:16:15.915 --> 00:16:17.085
also be waiting, sir.

00:16:29.065 --> 00:16:31.305
- Salute. Unity! - Unity!

00:17:08.435 --> 00:17:09.535
Requesting to return to duty.

00:17:35.565 --> 00:17:37.065
Oh, this place has great coffee.

00:17:37.235 --> 00:17:40.135
- I thought our coffee was the best. - It's in a class of its own!

00:17:40.335 --> 00:17:43.035
Gosh, look at the shine on this car.

00:17:43.605 --> 00:17:45.245
Driver Kim is going to love this.

00:17:47.105 --> 00:17:50.375
- The number you dialled is off... - Why is his phone off again?

00:18:28.315 --> 00:18:35.495
(2 weeks later)

00:19:03.855 --> 00:19:04.855
Is this it?

00:19:05.985 --> 00:19:08.025
Yes, this is the taxi Driver Kim was driving.

00:19:08.095 --> 00:19:11.155
For him to just abandon his taxi, something serious must've happened.

00:19:11.295 --> 00:19:12.895
Exactly. And his phone's been off this whole time.

00:19:13.225 --> 00:19:15.195
For now, could you two take the taxi back?

00:19:15.495 --> 00:19:17.335
I'll grab the nearby CCTV footage and then head back.

00:19:19.635 --> 00:19:21.065
It looks like he's paying his respect, doesn't it?

00:19:23.935 --> 00:19:27.505
Sergeant Yoo Sun A. She served with Driver Kim Do Gi.

00:19:27.575 --> 00:19:28.575
Sergeant?

00:19:29.075 --> 00:19:30.445
But she's a Master Sergeant in that photo.

00:19:30.645 --> 00:19:33.745
The records say she went AWOL from a training site...

00:19:34.245 --> 00:19:36.055
and died in an explosion while fleeing.

00:19:36.715 --> 00:19:40.255
She was posthumously disciplined and discharged as a private.

00:19:40.355 --> 00:19:41.925
Wait, that's a little strange.

00:19:42.825 --> 00:19:44.625
No matter how severe the disciplinary action,

00:19:44.925 --> 00:19:47.895
to demote someone that many ranks is highly unusual, isn't it?

00:19:48.095 --> 00:19:51.295
Seriously, what could she have possibly done?

00:19:51.935 --> 00:19:55.535
Either way, it seems Do Gi disappeared because of this,

00:19:56.535 --> 00:20:00.105
but I'm just wondering if looking for him now...

00:20:00.375 --> 00:20:02.275
is the right thing to do.

00:20:03.875 --> 00:20:05.845
That's been weighing on my mind too.

00:20:07.185 --> 00:20:09.015
From the way he even ditched his phone,

00:20:09.315 --> 00:20:12.225
Driver Kim didn't go missing. He chose to leave.

00:20:13.155 --> 00:20:15.025
It's almost like he's telling us not to look for him.

00:20:21.325 --> 00:20:23.195
Have a safe trip. See you tomorrow.

00:20:23.595 --> 00:20:25.165
Yes, see you tomorrow.

00:20:31.505 --> 00:20:33.475
He said he'd see me tomorrow.

00:21:06.275 --> 00:21:07.505
Mr. Jang, did you send this page?

00:21:07.645 --> 00:21:10.145
No, I just got the page and rushed down here.

00:21:10.745 --> 00:21:11.745
Go Eun, was it you?

00:21:12.485 --> 00:21:14.145
If none of us sent it,

00:21:15.615 --> 00:21:17.485
then this message must have come from Do Gi.

00:21:18.085 --> 00:21:20.285
But why send a page instead of just showing up?

00:21:20.825 --> 00:21:21.925
Maybe so we wouldn't worry?

00:21:22.395 --> 00:21:24.295
Then he would've called, not sent a page.

00:21:24.355 --> 00:21:26.765
Something must've happened to Driver Kim.

00:21:27.125 --> 00:21:29.095
We have to go find him right now.

00:21:29.195 --> 00:21:31.435
I agree. We have to. We absolutely have to go!

00:21:31.565 --> 00:21:34.875
Of course I want to go. But we don't know where he is.

00:21:36.435 --> 00:21:38.035
I did some more digging.

00:21:39.175 --> 00:21:43.015
Master Sergeant Yoo's last unit was a temp one, Unit 280.

00:21:43.215 --> 00:21:44.215
And there's one more thing.

00:21:45.115 --> 00:21:48.115
This is the exact spot where Driver Kim sent a page.

00:21:48.615 --> 00:21:49.755
But there's nothing there.

00:21:49.885 --> 00:21:53.825
That's right. The area's blurred out on Street View.

00:21:54.385 --> 00:21:55.425
It has to be a military base.

00:21:55.495 --> 00:21:59.225
In that case, that's most likely where Do Gi is right now.

00:21:59.665 --> 00:22:02.695
CEO, you once said that there are victims,

00:22:02.765 --> 00:22:05.835
but no perpetrators in two places. Hospitals and the military.

00:22:07.405 --> 00:22:08.675
We have to find Driver Kim now.

00:22:10.205 --> 00:22:12.075
But how do we get onto a military base?

00:22:12.145 --> 00:22:13.675
Civilians can't just go waltzing in there.

00:22:14.375 --> 00:22:16.645
It's a problem. What on earth are we going to do?

00:22:17.275 --> 00:22:19.545
Hey, Go Eun. Any bright ideas?

00:22:19.845 --> 00:22:22.555
The military? I know nothing.

00:22:22.855 --> 00:22:23.885
What would...

00:22:24.655 --> 00:22:26.655
Driver Kim do if he were here right now?

00:22:26.985 --> 00:22:29.825
If Driver Kim were here...

00:22:32.495 --> 00:22:33.825
I think I know what he would've done.

00:22:34.835 --> 00:22:35.835
What?

00:22:40.605 --> 00:22:41.605
Chief Park.

00:22:44.735 --> 00:22:46.075
I'll let you punch me 100 times.

00:22:46.675 --> 00:22:47.675
What?

00:22:48.815 --> 00:22:51.515
- Go Eun. - No, wait, make that 200.

00:22:51.945 --> 00:22:53.645
An Go Eun!

00:22:57.555 --> 00:23:00.455
- No way. I refuse to go. - Why refuse without knowing?

00:23:00.655 --> 00:23:02.555
I don't have to. I already know what she's about to say.

00:23:03.525 --> 00:23:05.495
You're going to ask me to re-enlist, aren't you?

00:23:06.165 --> 00:23:07.165
No.

00:23:08.795 --> 00:23:10.035
Whenever you feel like it,

00:23:10.995 --> 00:23:12.205
you can hit me for the rest of your life.

00:23:12.405 --> 00:23:16.135
No way. I can't. I won't. Absolutely not!

00:23:16.235 --> 00:23:17.705
Please just hit me!

00:23:23.775 --> 00:23:26.345
I'm not going. I can't go!

00:23:27.215 --> 00:23:29.985
Over my dead body!

00:23:50.975 --> 00:23:53.375
(Warning: Failure to comply will be met with fire.)

00:23:53.445 --> 00:23:55.745
(For our country and our people)

00:24:01.085 --> 00:24:02.554
We've filled personnel shortages.

00:24:02.555 --> 00:24:03.985
We got transfers for supply and mess,

00:24:04.055 --> 00:24:05.455
and one of them is a new recruit.

00:24:08.625 --> 00:24:11.025
- Private First Class Park Jin Su. - Private First Class Park Jin Su.

00:24:11.425 --> 00:24:12.465
Put your bag down.

00:24:13.525 --> 00:24:14.625
Run in place.

00:24:15.865 --> 00:24:16.865
Run.

00:24:21.265 --> 00:24:24.575
- Gosh, this is the last one. - Is this the army or a summer camp?

00:24:25.805 --> 00:24:27.375
You've all been through a lot getting here.

00:24:27.675 --> 00:24:29.675
From now on, this is your home.

00:24:33.545 --> 00:24:36.115
- Take them to their barracks. - Right this way.

00:24:36.515 --> 00:24:37.515
Yes, sir.

00:24:40.355 --> 00:24:41.355
That's right.

00:24:41.825 --> 00:24:43.495
I came here to find Driver Kim Do Gi.

00:24:44.495 --> 00:24:45.825
Once I find him, this will all be over.

00:24:46.965 --> 00:24:48.265
What's with that guy?

00:24:49.265 --> 00:24:50.795
I heard he just re-enlisted.

00:24:51.395 --> 00:24:55.735
Excuse me. I'm actually looking for someone.

00:24:55.975 --> 00:24:58.945
- Is there a Captain Kim Do Gi here? - Has this guy gone mad?

00:24:59.245 --> 00:25:01.175
What? Is the captain your buddy?

00:25:01.505 --> 00:25:02.515
That's right.

00:25:02.845 --> 00:25:06.315
We're the same age, so I act casual, but he keeps things formal.

00:25:07.545 --> 00:25:09.055
I think there's been a misunderstanding.

00:25:09.415 --> 00:25:13.925
I know the army pretty well. My service number starts with 11.

00:25:14.255 --> 00:25:16.295
What about you two? What do yours start with?

00:25:17.995 --> 00:25:19.065
What's the status?

00:25:20.365 --> 00:25:21.425
Still no word from him?

00:25:21.735 --> 00:25:23.695
Yes, his comms are still off.

00:25:23.995 --> 00:25:27.035
- I bet it's still in his bag. - Don't worry.

00:25:27.635 --> 00:25:29.435
Jin Eon will be doing just fine.

00:25:30.275 --> 00:25:31.435
This isn't his first rodeo.

00:25:35.145 --> 00:25:36.675
I was wrong, sir!

00:25:37.445 --> 00:25:40.585
I forgot I was in the army!

00:25:41.585 --> 00:25:43.115
I was wrong!

00:25:46.185 --> 00:25:47.825
What? You "forgot"?

00:25:48.695 --> 00:25:50.395
Hey, this jerk...

00:25:50.855 --> 00:25:52.795
When he's done with his punishment, throw him in the brig.

00:25:54.325 --> 00:25:55.465
I'm sorry!

00:25:55.865 --> 00:25:59.635
I was wrong! I'm sorry!

00:26:04.235 --> 00:26:06.875
So I guess facing the military alone is impossible after all?

00:26:08.175 --> 00:26:10.345
Looks like I'll have to go in myself.

00:26:11.015 --> 00:26:12.015
You, sir?

00:26:12.115 --> 00:26:14.585
Security's going to be tight there. How do you plan on getting in?

00:26:14.785 --> 00:26:18.055
When you get to be my age, it's not that hard.

00:26:23.055 --> 00:26:24.055
Halt.

00:26:24.225 --> 00:26:25.395
(For our country and our people)

00:26:26.295 --> 00:26:28.225
(For our country and our people)

00:26:34.565 --> 00:26:36.835
Sir. May I ask what brings you here?

00:26:37.275 --> 00:26:40.305
What kind of question is that? I'm here to see you do your job.

00:26:40.745 --> 00:26:41.875
What is it? Who's that?

00:26:43.275 --> 00:26:45.345
- And you are, sir? - Me?

00:26:46.085 --> 00:26:47.085
General...

00:26:47.785 --> 00:26:49.055
Unity!

00:26:50.215 --> 00:26:54.055
What are you gawking at? Are you opening this gate or what?

00:26:55.325 --> 00:26:56.595
Hey, you want me to just leave?

00:26:57.525 --> 00:26:59.425
- What is it? Who is he? - He's a general!

00:26:59.965 --> 00:27:00.995
My apologies, sir!

00:27:01.365 --> 00:27:02.835
What are you doing? Open the gate for him, now!

00:27:07.305 --> 00:27:09.235
- Salute! - Unity!

00:27:09.435 --> 00:27:10.475
All right. Carry on.

00:27:10.535 --> 00:27:12.175
(For our country and our people)

00:27:12.705 --> 00:27:14.745
- Guard post, comsec. - What is it?

00:27:14.805 --> 00:27:16.875
- A VIP's on base. - On the ground!

00:27:17.115 --> 00:27:18.115
- Sir! - Sir!

00:27:18.215 --> 00:27:20.515
- On your feet! - Sir!

00:27:21.285 --> 00:27:22.915
(Special mission code of conduct)

00:27:27.285 --> 00:27:28.755
(Garrison)

00:27:28.825 --> 00:27:30.755
(Rear supply unit)

00:27:33.595 --> 00:27:35.265
(Operational plan)

00:27:35.795 --> 00:27:37.865
Getting some screenshots.

00:27:44.005 --> 00:27:46.605
(Executive meeting, senior staff meeting minutes)

00:27:53.085 --> 00:27:56.385
- Unity! - As you were.

00:27:58.415 --> 00:27:59.624
The commander...

00:27:59.625 --> 00:28:01.385
The commander has stepped out, sir.

00:28:01.725 --> 00:28:02.725
I see.

00:28:04.525 --> 00:28:05.925
So, you're not going to ask why I'm here?

00:28:06.265 --> 00:28:08.025
First Lieutenant Lee Hyung In.

00:28:08.425 --> 00:28:10.665
With all due respect, sir, may I ask what brings you here?

00:28:11.035 --> 00:28:13.765
What do you think? I'm here to see my son.

00:28:14.905 --> 00:28:17.075
You have a new recruit here named Park Jin Eon, don't you?

00:28:17.505 --> 00:28:18.505
Park Jin Eon?

00:28:19.975 --> 00:28:21.475
I'll go myself...

00:28:23.115 --> 00:28:24.175
and bring him here.

00:28:24.675 --> 00:28:26.915
- Go ahead. - Unity.

00:28:27.615 --> 00:28:28.615
Unity.

00:28:41.625 --> 00:28:43.165
(Sgt. Yoo Sun A and seven others)

00:28:43.235 --> 00:28:45.935
Looks like there's something useful for us here.

00:28:46.305 --> 00:28:49.305
There's no information here besides Area B24.

00:28:49.605 --> 00:28:52.875
It's nearing the Demarcation Line. This is unsettling.

00:28:54.445 --> 00:28:58.045
Anyway, I'll do everything I can to find Driver Kim.

00:29:00.185 --> 00:29:04.215
But I bet Mr. Jang has no idea where to even begin.

00:29:05.455 --> 00:29:08.595
Instead of just sitting around here, we should go in and help find him.

00:29:09.395 --> 00:29:10.625
Into the military base? Us?

00:29:11.155 --> 00:29:12.295
And how are we supposed to get in?

00:29:16.265 --> 00:29:17.565
We'll just waltz right in, of course.

00:29:18.335 --> 00:29:19.335
What?

00:29:20.065 --> 00:29:22.205
And get a warm welcome while we're at it.

00:29:23.935 --> 00:29:24.935
What?

00:29:28.915 --> 00:29:29.975
(Special Mission Unit Rules of Conduct)

00:29:30.045 --> 00:29:31.115
(Special Mission Code of Conduct)

00:29:31.175 --> 00:29:32.485
Unity.

00:29:33.045 --> 00:29:34.415
Unity!

00:29:37.315 --> 00:29:39.125
- You little punk! - Mr. Jang?

00:29:40.555 --> 00:29:41.585
It's your old man.

00:29:42.655 --> 00:29:44.355
My dad?

00:29:53.505 --> 00:29:54.505
Let me get a good look at you.

00:29:54.965 --> 00:29:58.875
You little punk. You've gotten all chubby.

00:29:59.245 --> 00:30:01.245
Looks like the army life suits you, you little rascal.

00:30:03.915 --> 00:30:06.545
Stand up straight. Lead the way.

00:30:06.945 --> 00:30:08.885
Show your old man around the base, will you?

00:30:09.015 --> 00:30:12.085
- Then I can escort you... - No. If I asked for that,

00:30:12.155 --> 00:30:14.425
- I'd be pulling rank. - Lieutenant...

00:30:14.485 --> 00:30:16.755
Lead the way. Go on, you little punk.

00:30:17.525 --> 00:30:20.764
- Unity. - Hurry up, punk. Keep it up.

00:30:20.765 --> 00:30:21.964
One, two.

00:30:21.965 --> 00:30:22.965
Let's get a move on.

00:30:33.775 --> 00:30:35.415
Unity. This is First Lieutenant Lee Hyung In.

00:30:35.815 --> 00:30:37.975
It appears a general officer just arrived.

00:30:38.245 --> 00:30:39.945
A general? Why would one come to our unit?

00:30:40.315 --> 00:30:42.955
- He said he's here to see his son. - What are you talking about?

00:30:43.615 --> 00:30:46.885
If a general's son were in our unit, I'd know about it.

00:30:47.325 --> 00:30:48.655
He insists that it's his son...

00:30:49.195 --> 00:30:51.595
- I'll look into it. Hang up. - Unity.

00:30:54.025 --> 00:30:55.635
He did call him a little punk, though.

00:30:56.195 --> 00:30:59.035
Corporal Ma, do you listen to Elements?

00:30:59.235 --> 00:31:00.335
They're awesome.

00:31:00.765 --> 00:31:03.375
Elements? They're sick. They're my all-time favourite.

00:31:06.545 --> 00:31:08.675
(Armed Forces Welfare Agency)

00:31:08.745 --> 00:31:10.375
(Unity Club)

00:31:10.445 --> 00:31:12.845
(For our country and our people)

00:31:14.015 --> 00:31:15.485
How did a convenience store get all the way out here?

00:31:15.955 --> 00:31:17.615
I never thought we'd see one at a temporary post.

00:31:18.215 --> 00:31:19.285
Come on. Let's check it out.

00:31:19.355 --> 00:31:20.755
(Temporary Post: Unit for a specific mission)

00:31:22.025 --> 00:31:23.355
(Stop)

00:31:24.825 --> 00:31:26.865
- Hello, sir. - Yes, sir.

00:31:36.605 --> 00:31:38.535
- I'll go check over here. - All right.

00:31:40.775 --> 00:31:41.975
Driver Kim, are you in there?

00:31:51.585 --> 00:31:54.125
Hey, form a line! One at a time.

00:31:54.185 --> 00:31:56.895
You're going to hit it with your rifle. Gosh, look at these guys.

00:31:57.495 --> 00:31:59.795
- Get out of the way. - Let's go.

00:32:02.565 --> 00:32:04.195
- Thanks. - I'll take this one.

00:32:05.135 --> 00:32:06.405
Go Eun, now!

00:32:06.635 --> 00:32:09.635
(Armed Forces Welfare Agency, Unity Club)

00:32:11.775 --> 00:32:13.775
(Special Mission Code of Conduct)

00:32:16.775 --> 00:32:18.145
Unity, sir.

00:32:23.485 --> 00:32:24.485
You're a new face.

00:32:25.755 --> 00:32:27.824
- What's your unit? - I'm from the Intel Division.

00:32:27.825 --> 00:32:29.225
I'm here for a system check.

00:32:29.595 --> 00:32:30.625
I see.

00:32:31.955 --> 00:32:33.765
- First Lieutenant? - Yes, sir.

00:32:37.435 --> 00:32:38.565
And I'm a Captain.

00:32:42.635 --> 00:32:44.175
First Lieutenant An Go Eun.

00:32:48.915 --> 00:32:49.945
Appreciate all your hard work.

00:32:54.915 --> 00:32:57.355
- What do you think you're doing? - Is something wrong, sir?

00:32:57.415 --> 00:32:59.185
I said, what are you doing?

00:32:59.325 --> 00:33:01.555
I thought it was the right greeting for this unit.

00:33:02.125 --> 00:33:03.195
I was just following your lead.

00:33:05.865 --> 00:33:08.465
- Did that bother you? - Has she lost her darn mind?

00:33:08.525 --> 00:33:10.165
If you don't like it,

00:33:10.835 --> 00:33:13.535
then don't treat people like that.

00:33:14.335 --> 00:33:15.335
Got it?

00:33:17.975 --> 00:33:19.175
Unity.

00:33:20.745 --> 00:33:21.775
Darn it.

00:33:23.445 --> 00:33:24.545
Unity.

00:33:25.815 --> 00:33:28.585
- Unity. Yes, Commander. - Unity.

00:33:29.455 --> 00:33:32.255
Captain Kim Do Gi should have reported here recently.

00:33:32.725 --> 00:33:33.925
Let me check for you, ma'am.

00:33:34.625 --> 00:33:35.625
Driver Kim Do Gi.

00:33:38.655 --> 00:33:39.765
Driver Kim, you in there?

00:33:40.025 --> 00:33:41.095
Do Gi, are you there?

00:33:44.995 --> 00:33:46.835
- I don't think he's here. - Let's check the next floor up.

00:33:46.865 --> 00:33:48.605
- Okay. - Yes.

00:33:49.305 --> 00:33:50.835
Yes, I understand. Unity.

00:33:54.275 --> 00:33:55.305
Hey.

00:33:55.675 --> 00:33:59.385
HQ says no general's son was sent to our unit.

00:34:00.645 --> 00:34:02.355
So who did you just let in?

00:34:02.755 --> 00:34:03.755
Sir?

00:34:06.685 --> 00:34:08.055
(Soldier's Personnel File)

00:34:08.925 --> 00:34:11.795
You punk, where is your head at?

00:34:13.065 --> 00:34:14.725
Go catch that darn impostor now!

00:34:15.295 --> 00:34:17.995
Yes, sir. Unity!

00:34:19.465 --> 00:34:20.665
Darn it.

00:34:28.505 --> 00:34:30.545
Now what is that? Darn it.

00:34:34.115 --> 00:34:35.285
Unity.

00:34:38.155 --> 00:34:39.155
Go Eun.

00:34:39.925 --> 00:34:43.025
- How did you get in here? - I just waltzed right in.

00:34:44.055 --> 00:34:45.055
And...

00:34:45.565 --> 00:34:46.565
What?

00:34:47.495 --> 00:34:49.495
These are the keys to the Deluxe Taxi.

00:34:49.695 --> 00:34:51.365
Driver Kim was here.

00:34:57.535 --> 00:34:59.205
All right, anyone seen our Driver Kim Do Gi...

00:34:59.645 --> 00:35:01.505
I mean, Captain Kim Do Gi? Raise your hand if you've seen him.

00:35:01.775 --> 00:35:03.345
You'll get a free box of soy milk.

00:35:03.915 --> 00:35:05.444
Me, sir!

00:35:05.445 --> 00:35:07.645
- I have. - You've seen Captain Kim Do Gi?

00:35:07.745 --> 00:35:11.955
- I'm the one who cleans his room. - Come out and get your free case.

00:35:12.015 --> 00:35:13.455
(Vegemil High-Protein Soy Milk)

00:35:13.525 --> 00:35:15.455
(Armed Forces Welfare Agency, Unity Club)

00:35:21.025 --> 00:35:22.495
Unity.

00:35:25.065 --> 00:35:27.665
Take us to Captain Kim Do Gi's room, and I'll give you another free box.

00:35:27.735 --> 00:35:29.405
- Everyone, stand back! - Move!

00:35:29.475 --> 00:35:30.575
- Out of the way! - Move it!

00:35:30.875 --> 00:35:32.775
- Hey, what's going on? - Move aside! Get out!

00:35:32.845 --> 00:35:33.845
Don't shoot!

00:35:34.145 --> 00:35:37.745
I'll tell you anything! Ask one thing, I'll tell you two!

00:35:37.815 --> 00:35:39.715
Just don't shoot!

00:35:39.785 --> 00:35:41.715
(Establishing Military Discipline, The 2802nd Unit)

00:35:45.555 --> 00:35:47.685
Mr. Jang! Jin Eon, Go Eun!

00:35:48.355 --> 00:35:49.455
Are you guys here to rescue me?

00:35:50.695 --> 00:35:51.895
We got captured too!

00:35:52.325 --> 00:35:53.465
Right.

00:35:54.225 --> 00:35:55.595
Please don't shoot!

00:35:57.595 --> 00:35:59.805
So these jerks are all in on it together.

00:36:02.005 --> 00:36:03.175
Who are you people?

00:36:04.075 --> 00:36:05.645
I'm only going to ask you this one more time.

00:36:06.675 --> 00:36:07.745
Who are you people?

00:36:14.015 --> 00:36:15.015
(Unity Club)

00:36:15.085 --> 00:36:17.715
(Welcome)

00:36:37.375 --> 00:36:38.575
What took you all so long?

00:36:40.845 --> 00:36:41.845
Do Gi.

00:36:44.575 --> 00:36:45.985
Glad you could all make it.

00:37:02.095 --> 00:37:05.495
(2 weeks earlier)

00:37:05.565 --> 00:37:09.405
(2 weeks earlier)

00:37:09.675 --> 00:37:12.405
It's in the Civilian Control Zone, so I'll need military credentials.

00:37:13.075 --> 00:37:15.814
A company-grade officer...

00:37:15.815 --> 00:37:17.745
can only re-enlist within three years of leaving.

00:37:19.045 --> 00:37:21.785
But you're well past that deadline.

00:37:23.055 --> 00:37:25.215
Even if we get you in, it'll be flagged immediately.

00:37:26.285 --> 00:37:28.685
So forget the two weeks you asked for.

00:37:29.255 --> 00:37:32.095
You won't even last two days before it's voided.

00:37:34.065 --> 00:37:35.065
Here.

00:37:44.005 --> 00:37:48.775
An endangered Black Eagle's nest was found in the border region.

00:37:48.845 --> 00:37:49.915
(Eagle Nest Found, Border Region Emergency Survey)

00:37:49.975 --> 00:37:52.685
So we need someone to spend three weeks...

00:37:52.985 --> 00:37:54.615
identifying and surveying the habitat.

00:37:56.085 --> 00:37:57.085
How about it?

00:37:57.785 --> 00:37:59.625
Think you can handle it?

00:38:01.855 --> 00:38:05.595
Thank you. I won't burden you any further.

00:38:06.025 --> 00:38:09.435
Burden? Not at all. I'm the one asking for a favour.

00:38:10.065 --> 00:38:12.635
Okay. Take that car back there.

00:38:13.105 --> 00:38:14.565
Everything you need is in there.

00:38:15.035 --> 00:38:16.035
Yes, sir.

00:39:07.385 --> 00:39:08.885
Halt!

00:39:09.555 --> 00:39:10.555
Lights off.

00:39:11.325 --> 00:39:12.325
Engine off.

00:39:13.825 --> 00:39:14.995
Driver, exit the vehicle.

00:39:19.365 --> 00:39:20.365
Turtle.

00:39:21.135 --> 00:39:22.905
- Ladder. - Who goes there?

00:39:25.005 --> 00:39:26.305
Captain Kim Do Gi.

00:39:26.805 --> 00:39:27.845
State your business.

00:39:28.745 --> 00:39:30.975
On assignment. I've spoken with the duty commander.

00:39:31.875 --> 00:39:34.745
- Captain Kim Do Gi has arrived. - Yes, let him through.

00:39:35.615 --> 00:39:36.655
Yes, sir.

00:39:37.515 --> 00:39:40.255
- Copy that. - Identity confirmed. Unity.

00:39:40.655 --> 00:39:41.685
Unity.

00:40:25.635 --> 00:40:26.665
Unity.

00:40:27.535 --> 00:40:30.405
We weren't expecting you today, so your room isn't ready yet.

00:40:30.775 --> 00:40:32.175
We were told you'd be arriving tomorrow.

00:40:37.575 --> 00:40:40.015
Don't worry about it. I can sleep anywhere.

00:40:41.315 --> 00:40:43.915
So, what mission are you here for?

00:40:44.085 --> 00:40:46.655
I'll brief the unit commander on the details tomorrow.

00:40:47.485 --> 00:40:49.355
Is the office all set up?

00:40:50.925 --> 00:40:51.925
Yes, sir.

00:41:14.885 --> 00:41:19.285
You of all people know what Sergeant Yoo Sun A was like.

00:41:19.385 --> 00:41:20.385
(Petition)

00:41:20.485 --> 00:41:21.555
(Victim: The late Sgt. Yoo Sun A)

00:41:23.995 --> 00:41:25.125
I'll be in touch.

00:41:27.425 --> 00:41:29.195
I'd like you to come back then.

00:41:29.865 --> 00:41:30.865
Understood.

00:41:36.975 --> 00:41:39.205
- He came last night? - Yes, sir.

00:41:40.645 --> 00:41:42.275
So where is he now?

00:41:42.505 --> 00:41:45.045
He wanted his own room, so I gave him one of the empty ones.

00:41:45.175 --> 00:41:46.645
He said he'd introduce himself this morning.

00:41:46.815 --> 00:41:48.545
He should just do his job and leave.

00:41:48.885 --> 00:41:50.455
What's the point of an introduction?

00:41:57.825 --> 00:42:00.195
Unity. Apologies for the late introduction.

00:42:00.525 --> 00:42:02.935
Yes. You had a long trip.

00:42:03.695 --> 00:42:05.735
- I hear you arrived last night. - Yes, sir.

00:42:06.405 --> 00:42:08.705
The room's great, by the way. It gets a good breeze.

00:42:10.135 --> 00:42:11.135
Right.

00:42:11.635 --> 00:42:12.805
And the reason for your assignment is?

00:42:12.845 --> 00:42:14.345
(Colonel Kim Tae Hyun)

00:42:19.385 --> 00:42:20.445
(Eagle Nest Found, Border Region Emergency Survey)

00:42:20.515 --> 00:42:21.585
(Urgent Survey Team to the Border Region)

00:42:21.645 --> 00:42:22.645
Surveying birds?

00:42:23.685 --> 00:42:24.685
Yes, sir.

00:42:25.485 --> 00:42:26.525
What kind of bird?

00:42:27.055 --> 00:42:29.255
- Black Eagle, sir. - It's an eagle?

00:42:29.325 --> 00:42:32.625
They were thought to be extinct, but a nest was recently found.

00:42:33.765 --> 00:42:34.765
But...

00:42:35.625 --> 00:42:38.295
- why send you for a bird survey? - I may not know about birds,

00:42:38.735 --> 00:42:41.165
but I know the border ecosystem very well.

00:42:43.375 --> 00:42:44.935
So what happens if you find this bird here?

00:42:45.275 --> 00:42:47.605
It's an endangered species, so we'd have to protect it.

00:42:48.645 --> 00:42:50.845
So if it becomes a protected area, we can't fire our weapons?

00:42:51.675 --> 00:42:53.085
That's highly likely.

00:42:55.285 --> 00:42:57.255
We're better off if it's not here, even if it is, right?

00:43:00.425 --> 00:43:04.695
Anyway, if you need anything, let me know, okay?

00:43:05.655 --> 00:43:07.025
This is my house,

00:43:07.495 --> 00:43:10.095
so don't go wandering around like you own the place.

00:43:11.435 --> 00:43:12.865
Thanks for your consideration.

00:43:13.805 --> 00:43:15.005
Right. Do you need anything?

00:43:15.805 --> 00:43:17.275
Do you want me to assign a soldier to you?

00:43:17.535 --> 00:43:19.645
That's all right. I've already called someone in.

00:43:24.415 --> 00:43:25.445
Unity!

00:43:26.045 --> 00:43:28.785
Speak of the devil. He'll be rooming with me,

00:43:28.845 --> 00:43:29.985
so you don't have to worry about a thing.

00:43:30.255 --> 00:43:31.255
Yes, sir.

00:43:32.315 --> 00:43:33.685
I haven't eaten yet,

00:43:34.055 --> 00:43:37.355
so if you haven't either, would you care to join me?

00:43:37.795 --> 00:43:38.795
I'm good.

00:43:39.495 --> 00:43:42.765
There's a jjamppong place near the entrance. It's really good.

00:43:42.965 --> 00:43:43.995
You should go try it.

00:43:44.365 --> 00:43:45.895
Thanks for the tip.

00:43:47.765 --> 00:43:48.765
Unity.

00:44:02.215 --> 00:44:04.115
(Advanced barracks, elite special forces)

00:44:04.185 --> 00:44:05.955
(Establishing discipline, accomplishing the mission)

00:44:06.015 --> 00:44:07.855
Captain, I knew you'd call on me,

00:44:08.425 --> 00:44:11.525
but I never imagined it would be for something like this.

00:44:12.155 --> 00:44:14.164
- Let's get food first. - Yes, sir.

00:44:14.165 --> 00:44:15.465
- You drive. - Yes, sir.

00:44:22.605 --> 00:44:23.605
Hey.

00:44:23.705 --> 00:44:25.705
What do you think they're really here for?

00:44:26.445 --> 00:44:28.575
He said he was here for the protected species research.

00:44:29.645 --> 00:44:31.545
"Protected species," my foot.

00:44:31.975 --> 00:44:32.985
You don't think so?

00:44:33.045 --> 00:44:36.415
He was a Special Warfare instructor, he's led operations,

00:44:36.715 --> 00:44:40.025
and he quit after years of overseas intel.

00:44:40.655 --> 00:44:42.385
You think he's here for birds? Give me a break.

00:44:43.695 --> 00:44:47.365
Tail those jerks and find out what they're really up to.

00:44:48.225 --> 00:44:49.935
- Dig in. - Yes, sir. You too.

00:44:59.505 --> 00:45:00.645
This jjamppong is pretty good.

00:45:01.075 --> 00:45:02.075
It is, sir.

00:45:04.145 --> 00:45:07.345
I looked over the internal report on Master Sergeant Yoo's charges.

00:45:09.045 --> 00:45:10.054
During a training exercise,

00:45:10.055 --> 00:45:11.685
Master Sergeant Yoo abandoned her squad...

00:45:12.615 --> 00:45:15.755
and drove a truck full of weapons into North Korea.

00:45:15.825 --> 00:45:17.095
No way...

00:45:18.255 --> 00:45:19.295
That's impossible.

00:45:21.395 --> 00:45:23.935
Going AWOL from the training site, theft of weapons,

00:45:25.095 --> 00:45:26.965
and attempting to contact North Korean officials.

00:45:29.705 --> 00:45:33.275
She was demoted three ranks, one for each charge.

00:45:34.775 --> 00:45:35.905
Captain, do you...

00:45:37.045 --> 00:45:40.085
really believe Master Sergeant Yoo would do something like that?

00:45:42.615 --> 00:45:44.055
Could you do it, Master Sergeant Park?

00:45:45.685 --> 00:45:48.425
Commandeering a truck, stealing strategic weapons,

00:45:48.955 --> 00:45:52.855
and coordinating a time and date with a North Korean operative.

00:45:55.695 --> 00:45:57.465
All in less than a week of being deployed here?

00:45:58.595 --> 00:45:59.865
I don't think even I could pull that off.

00:46:09.775 --> 00:46:13.645
Quietly meet with the squad members who were with Master Sergeant Yoo.

00:46:14.245 --> 00:46:17.685
All eyes will be on me for a while, so you shouldn't have any trouble.

00:46:18.215 --> 00:46:19.255
Yes, sir.

00:46:19.585 --> 00:46:23.695
One more thing. Do senior officers get temp posts?

00:46:23.755 --> 00:46:24.755
No, sir.

00:46:25.625 --> 00:46:27.365
Actually, I thought that was strange too.

00:46:27.695 --> 00:46:30.435
A colonel living in the barracks instead of his own quarters...

00:46:30.495 --> 00:46:33.405
Isn't that pretty unprecedented?

00:46:36.135 --> 00:46:37.175
Exactly.

00:46:37.235 --> 00:46:40.445
So do we really have to look for this bird?

00:46:41.645 --> 00:46:43.815
Well, it's not like they're going to believe us anyway.

00:46:49.585 --> 00:46:51.415
Gosh, this jjamppong is really good.

00:46:51.655 --> 00:46:52.685
It's so good, sir.

00:46:53.455 --> 00:46:56.055
- Was that good? - Yes. Gosh, I'm stuffed.

00:46:56.455 --> 00:46:57.455
Good.

00:47:07.105 --> 00:47:09.005
Captain, where are you going?

00:47:22.115 --> 00:47:25.255
Looks like he's from my unit. Why is he taking my picture?

00:47:26.155 --> 00:47:27.285
I'm not a bird.

00:47:29.855 --> 00:47:31.755
Go tell your commanding officer.

00:47:36.595 --> 00:47:38.135
Unity! You called for me, sir?

00:47:39.095 --> 00:47:41.004
We got a message from Captain Kim Do Gi.

00:47:41.005 --> 00:47:42.005
We did?

00:47:42.405 --> 00:47:44.005
Hey, read it again.

00:47:45.335 --> 00:47:49.105
Your jjamppong suggestion was great. Please recommend more great spots.

00:47:49.245 --> 00:47:52.475
Also, I need a bird-watching camera, so I'll borrow this and return it.

00:47:52.545 --> 00:47:53.645
Thank you for being so thoughtful.

00:47:55.185 --> 00:47:56.354
No matter how you slice it,

00:47:56.355 --> 00:47:59.355
it looks like that jerk, Kim Do Gi, has an ulterior motive.

00:47:59.415 --> 00:48:02.725
- I'm sure of it. - I'll see what he's up to, sir.

00:48:04.725 --> 00:48:07.225
Report the second you find anything, even if it's at dawn.

00:48:07.295 --> 00:48:09.895
Yes, sir. Unity!

00:48:11.265 --> 00:48:12.265
- Unity! - Unity!

00:48:19.705 --> 00:48:21.575
(Investigation Team)

00:48:24.215 --> 00:48:26.745
All the squad members' statements match.

00:48:27.745 --> 00:48:29.144
They said on the way to the op zone,

00:48:29.145 --> 00:48:31.055
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A told them all to get out.

00:48:50.505 --> 00:48:51.505
Get out.

00:48:52.005 --> 00:48:54.075
- Get out now! - Yes, ma'am! Understood!

00:48:56.515 --> 00:48:58.045
Everyone, dismount the truck.

00:48:59.115 --> 00:49:00.115
Move it! Out!

00:49:00.685 --> 00:49:01.845
- Yes, ma'am! - Yes, ma'am!

00:49:08.125 --> 00:49:11.495
Effective immediately, you will all return to base.

00:49:12.095 --> 00:49:14.125
- We must have misheard you, ma'am. - You heard me, didn't you?

00:49:14.465 --> 00:49:15.625
Everyone, return to base!

00:49:15.965 --> 00:49:17.095
- Yes, ma'am! Understood! - Yes, ma'am! Understood!

00:49:23.005 --> 00:49:25.235
They didn't seem to be lying, sir.

00:49:28.205 --> 00:49:30.245
Could Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A really have done that?

00:49:30.645 --> 00:49:31.815
(Results: Explosion in Operation Area B-24)

00:49:34.215 --> 00:49:35.945
Those reasons listed for her demotion...

00:49:36.415 --> 00:49:38.955
Could they really be true?

00:49:39.985 --> 00:49:41.225
The answer to that...

00:49:42.755 --> 00:49:44.455
is one you've already given, Master Sergeant Park.

00:49:47.695 --> 00:49:48.795
Yes, you're right, sir.

00:49:49.095 --> 00:49:52.094
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A would never do that.

00:49:52.095 --> 00:49:53.605
I'm absolutely sure of it.

00:49:55.565 --> 00:49:56.875
I agree.

00:50:11.055 --> 00:50:12.055
Unity.

00:50:13.455 --> 00:50:14.455
Unity.

00:50:17.755 --> 00:50:20.125
Who's in charge of the vehicle movement logs?

00:50:21.125 --> 00:50:22.495
The transportation unit co-manages them.

00:50:22.565 --> 00:50:24.895
What's the logging interval? Every five minutes?

00:50:25.295 --> 00:50:26.365
Yes, sir, that's correct.

00:50:27.105 --> 00:50:28.205
And the reporting cycle to command?

00:50:28.265 --> 00:50:30.035
It's automatically updated every three weeks, sir.

00:50:30.405 --> 00:50:31.405
That's perfect.

00:50:32.905 --> 00:50:35.445
Get me a copy for this date.

00:50:35.805 --> 00:50:37.945
- Right now. - Right now, sir?

00:50:39.475 --> 00:50:41.785
You must be busy betting your pay in the barracks.

00:50:42.315 --> 00:50:43.385
Master Sergeant Park, why don't you get it?

00:50:43.655 --> 00:50:44.655
Yes, sir.

00:50:46.255 --> 00:50:47.655
Gambling on duty?

00:50:48.055 --> 00:50:50.195
He seems busy. I'll get it myself, sir.

00:50:50.725 --> 00:50:53.825
No, sir! I'll go get it right this second!

00:50:53.965 --> 00:50:56.635
Really? Then you'd better be quick about it.

00:50:58.365 --> 00:50:59.465
Yes, sir!

00:50:59.905 --> 00:51:02.105
- Unity! - About-face!

00:51:02.605 --> 00:51:03.935
On the double!

00:51:06.805 --> 00:51:09.405
By the way, Captain, how do you know all that?

00:51:09.705 --> 00:51:10.715
Know what?

00:51:10.775 --> 00:51:13.815
That vehicle movements are logged in five-minute intervals.

00:51:14.085 --> 00:51:16.485
They're mostly logged to evaluate training performance.

00:51:16.685 --> 00:51:19.655
- But isn't that data classified? - It is.

00:51:20.185 --> 00:51:23.425
But I'm the one who used to grade the performance evaluations.

00:51:23.995 --> 00:51:26.765
I reviewed those logs and gave you the best score.

00:51:30.035 --> 00:51:31.165
You did?

00:51:35.065 --> 00:51:36.105
Unity!

00:51:36.935 --> 00:51:38.975
These are the vehicle movement logs for the date you requested, sir.

00:51:40.545 --> 00:51:43.205
- Thanks. Good work. - Unity!

00:51:43.545 --> 00:51:47.185
- Unity. - Save your pay and be a good son.

00:51:48.545 --> 00:51:49.545
Unity!

00:51:58.155 --> 00:52:01.125
Let's use this to retrace her steps on the day of the incident.

00:52:02.725 --> 00:52:04.665
And see what she was trying to do.

00:52:04.735 --> 00:52:07.505
So that's why you asked for the logs from the day of the incident.

00:52:07.805 --> 00:52:08.805
You never know.

00:52:09.265 --> 00:52:12.435
Her route might tell us what happened that day.

00:52:13.275 --> 00:52:14.275
Right.

00:52:17.945 --> 00:52:19.115
Unity!

00:52:21.915 --> 00:52:22.945
Unity!

00:52:23.415 --> 00:52:27.555
You'd think people studying birds would have at least one photo.

00:52:28.725 --> 00:52:29.785
Is there a problem, Colonel?

00:52:30.225 --> 00:52:33.795
If you're here to investigate birds, you should be focused on them.

00:52:34.665 --> 00:52:36.735
So why are you digging into a dead woman's business?

00:52:42.335 --> 00:52:47.045
Why are you snooping on a traitor who betrayed her country?

00:52:49.605 --> 00:52:52.245
Since you've asked, allow me to ask you something.

00:52:56.955 --> 00:52:59.585
How did you know she was dealing with the North?

00:53:01.285 --> 00:53:04.395
- What? - You couldn't have met either side,

00:53:04.755 --> 00:53:08.795
- and you weren't there, were you? - Hey.

00:53:10.195 --> 00:53:12.565
Do you need to be next to a fire to know it's burning?

00:53:13.295 --> 00:53:16.675
You can tell there's a fire by the smoke from a distance.

00:53:17.375 --> 00:53:22.345
Aborting the mission on her own, disobeying orders, sending men back,

00:53:22.975 --> 00:53:26.315
then loading weapons into a truck and heading North. It's obvious.

00:53:26.815 --> 00:53:28.315
Just seeing that smoke,

00:53:28.385 --> 00:53:31.355
it's clear she was playing with fire, don't you think?

00:53:32.585 --> 00:53:34.055
I see your point.

00:53:36.925 --> 00:53:37.955
Hey, Kim Do Gi.

00:53:40.325 --> 00:53:42.795
- Yes, sir. - I'm sure I made myself clear.

00:53:43.125 --> 00:53:45.435
Don't come into my house and act like you own the place.

00:53:46.765 --> 00:53:48.735
What's your real reason for being here?

00:53:49.505 --> 00:53:50.505
Who sent you?

00:53:50.575 --> 00:53:53.575
I believe I already told you. A Black Eagle nest was discovered...

00:53:53.645 --> 00:53:55.545
Cut the nonsense, you jerk!

00:53:56.105 --> 00:53:57.575
Black Eagle, my foot!

00:54:03.245 --> 00:54:06.615
I have to get back to the nest, so if you'll excuse me.

00:54:08.085 --> 00:54:09.085
Unity!

00:54:11.525 --> 00:54:13.055
(Bird investigation)

00:54:14.895 --> 00:54:17.465
But I guess a bird's nest is someone else's home too.

00:54:18.865 --> 00:54:20.135
This is awkward.

00:54:23.005 --> 00:54:25.435
And by the way,

00:54:26.105 --> 00:54:27.905
people don't really put photos up on walls.

00:54:29.605 --> 00:54:30.945
Not when you have one of these.

00:54:38.815 --> 00:54:39.815
Unity!

00:54:47.025 --> 00:54:48.825
That arrogant jerk...

00:54:49.395 --> 00:54:51.265
A measly Captain has the nerve...

00:54:53.735 --> 00:54:55.005
Sir, what should we do?

00:54:57.105 --> 00:55:00.305
He must have someone backing him up to be so cocky, don't you think?

00:55:02.675 --> 00:55:04.575
I'm going to go see the General.

00:55:06.575 --> 00:55:08.615
(Special Warfare School)

00:55:23.265 --> 00:55:24.265
Stop here for a second.

00:55:25.095 --> 00:55:26.095
Yes, sir.

00:55:38.175 --> 00:55:39.175
What is it, Captain?

00:55:41.885 --> 00:55:43.584
On the day of the incident,

00:55:43.585 --> 00:55:45.285
Master Sergeant Yoo had her team exit the truck here.

00:55:45.915 --> 00:55:47.525
Everyone, dismount the truck.

00:55:48.525 --> 00:55:49.525
Move it! Out!

00:55:49.526 --> 00:55:50.625
- Yes, ma'am! - Yes, ma'am!

00:55:53.765 --> 00:55:55.325
She took the right fork.

00:55:58.495 --> 00:56:01.235
What? But this is Sector B24.

00:56:02.305 --> 00:56:04.405
Why? Is there a problem with that?

00:56:05.135 --> 00:56:07.604
On the day of Master Sergeant Yoo's accident,

00:56:07.605 --> 00:56:09.205
my team was also scheduled...

00:56:09.275 --> 00:56:11.075
with an artillery unit for a live-fire drill.

00:56:12.775 --> 00:56:16.215
And the target for that drill was right here, in Sector B24.

00:56:16.285 --> 00:56:17.655
(Military Demarcation Line, Special Mission Unit's Area of Ops)

00:56:33.095 --> 00:56:34.765
- Let's go. - Yes, sir.

00:56:51.255 --> 00:56:53.455
Sector B24 starts here.

00:57:32.295 --> 00:57:35.065
(Military Demarcation Line, Special Mission Unit's Area of Ops)

00:57:38.995 --> 00:57:40.665
(Special mission code of conduct)

00:58:19.675 --> 00:58:21.675
Master Sergeant Yoo was here for ten minutes.

00:58:30.715 --> 00:58:32.485
Only this spot right here is empty.

00:58:42.565 --> 00:58:45.465
It looks like she couldn't move everything on the shelf at once.

00:59:13.025 --> 00:59:14.864
Instead of going to the base,

00:59:14.865 --> 00:59:16.665
Master Sergeant Yoo went up this path to the north.

00:59:17.365 --> 00:59:19.735
Yes, that's what the report said.

00:59:20.035 --> 00:59:21.635
That she took the weapons north.

00:59:24.175 --> 00:59:26.775
Master Sergeant Yoo didn't go north to sell the weapons.

00:59:29.305 --> 00:59:31.315
Her original route back was blocked,

00:59:32.115 --> 00:59:33.345
so she couldn't get through.

00:59:33.675 --> 00:59:34.685
What?

00:59:53.135 --> 00:59:54.135
Darn it.

00:59:54.635 --> 00:59:57.975
Back off, you jerks! Are you disobeying a direct order?

01:00:04.715 --> 01:00:06.215
Since her escape route was blocked,

01:00:08.145 --> 01:00:10.045
she tried to find an alternate route.

01:00:10.555 --> 01:00:12.814
If she sought a new route, like you said,

01:00:12.815 --> 01:00:15.085
she had to be panicking.

01:00:15.425 --> 01:00:17.695
This path is a dead end at the Military Demarcation Line.

01:00:18.595 --> 01:00:21.025
And there's no way Master Sergeant Yoo didn't know that.

01:00:22.065 --> 01:00:24.195
Or did she head that way knowing it was a dead end?

01:00:24.965 --> 01:00:26.495
With her escape route blocked,

01:00:28.665 --> 01:00:31.435
Master Sergeant Yoo would have done the only thing she could.

01:00:32.605 --> 01:00:34.205
The only thing she could?

01:00:38.615 --> 01:00:39.675
Captain Kim Do Gi!

01:00:42.945 --> 01:00:44.215
I have a question.

01:00:45.385 --> 01:00:47.955
There are times in the field when our mission objective...

01:00:48.025 --> 01:00:50.155
is to acquire certain intelligence, right?

01:00:50.895 --> 01:00:52.095
There'll be plenty of those in the future.

01:00:52.355 --> 01:00:54.025
Let's say we've acquired critical intelligence,

01:00:54.225 --> 01:00:57.565
but on our way back to base, we run into an unavoidable problem.

01:00:58.235 --> 01:00:59.895
What do we do with the intel?

01:01:05.105 --> 01:01:06.935
Your safety comes before the intel.

01:01:07.745 --> 01:01:09.375
If your safety isn't guaranteed,

01:01:09.975 --> 01:01:11.545
you abandon the critical intelligence.

01:01:13.775 --> 01:01:14.845
But if, despite all that,

01:01:16.315 --> 01:01:18.785
you find yourself in a life-or-death situation,

01:01:19.685 --> 01:01:23.155
you pass on the intel using our team's protocol.

01:01:38.535 --> 01:01:42.045
(Landmine)

01:01:53.685 --> 01:01:56.125
Captain, you should watch your step.

01:02:03.465 --> 01:02:05.065
Master Sergeant Park, search this area.

01:02:05.095 --> 01:02:06.295
Yes, sir.

01:02:38.435 --> 01:02:40.835
What is that protocol?

01:02:41.365 --> 01:02:45.705
Find the bird's nest in the closest tree due west...

01:02:46.305 --> 01:02:47.505
and secure the intel inside it.

01:02:48.105 --> 01:02:49.245
A bird's nest?

01:02:50.675 --> 01:02:53.075
They're sturdy, they have good drainage,

01:02:54.685 --> 01:02:56.045
and they're hard to see from the ground.

01:02:58.055 --> 01:02:59.085
I see.

01:03:04.395 --> 01:03:05.395
Master Sergeant Park!

01:03:05.955 --> 01:03:06.955
Sir!

01:03:11.465 --> 01:03:12.535
I'll check it out.

01:03:25.445 --> 01:03:26.445
I found it.

01:03:55.005 --> 01:03:57.615
(Landmine)

01:04:46.725 --> 01:04:48.765
If anything should happen to me,

01:04:51.865 --> 01:04:53.765
I'm trusting you to find this.

01:04:54.305 --> 01:04:55.405
Captain Kim Do Gi.

01:05:15.325 --> 01:05:17.695
Master Sergeant Yoo Sun A sacrificed herself...

01:05:18.595 --> 01:05:19.895
to save her comrades.

01:06:08.875 --> 01:06:10.545
(Special thanks to Jeon So Nee for her guest appearance)